--- refinement — the contract/refinement predicate vocabulary.
---
--- This file is the Handl-authored source of truth for `Pred`: the symbolic
--- predicate language used by `requires:`/`guarantee:` clauses in `.hnl`
--- contract files (`str.hnl`, `time.hnl`, `rand.hnl`, `collection/*.hnl`,
--- `plugin-ext-refinement/contracts/*.hnl`). The decision (per user) is that
--- this vocabulary lives in Handl as a `data` declaration, not as a Rust
--- enum — `crates/plugin-ext-refinement/src/types.rs` `pub enum Pred`
--- currently *mirrors* it in Rust, pending full `data`-constructor eval
--- (indexed families are WIP, ADR-0082).
---
--- Consumption contract: `data` constructors evaluate to tagged records
--- `{"tag": "<ConstructorName>", "<arg>": <value>, ...}` — the `"tag"` key
--- carries the constructor name verbatim (e.g. `Sorted("xs")` evaluates to
--- `{"tag": "Sorted", "list": "xs"}`). This is the same encoding produced by
--- `desugar_data`/`data` eval (`crates/handl-runtime/tests/
--- data_constructor_eval.rs`: `Succ(Zero)` → `{"tag":"Succ","pred":{...}}`),
--- NOT the `__tag__` nominal-tag encoding used by `tag`/`result`.
--- Rust-side consumers translate `guarantee:` surface syntax into these
--- variants via `plugin-ext-refinement/src/loader.rs` `parse_named_pred`
--- (e.g. `Sorted(x)`, `LengthEq(a, b)`, `p && q`, `p || q`, `p ==> q`,
--- `forall x in list, p(x)`); constructor names and arities below match that
--- parser one-for-one.
---
--- Field annotations: `Name` is symbolic — it stands for a *variable name*
--- (a string identifying a program variable such as `x`, `output`, `a`),
--- matching the `String` payloads of the Rust enum. Handl `data` syntax has
--- no way to express "string that names a variable"; the annotation
--- documents intent only (like `String`/`Float` in `str.hnl`). `lhs`/`rhs`
--- fields of `And`/`Or`/`Implies` are recursive `Pred` payloads.
---
--- NOTE (format): this is a canonical-language file (parsed by the kit's
--- Pratt grammar + `desugar_data`), NOT a `parse_contracts` axiom file —
--- `plugin-ext-refinement`'s line-based loader only accepts `axiom` decls
--- and would reject `data`. The declaration must stay on ONE line: the
--- top-level statement splitter breaks at newlines, and wrapping the
--- alternatives in parens defeats `collect_constructors` (verified with
--- `hnl typecheck` / `hnl eval`).
---
--- NOTE (eval WIP): `hnl typecheck` passes on this file and `hnl eval` handles
--- any 17-constructor prefix, but evaluating all 18 constructors at once
--- currently OOMs — the desugared constructors each capture the growing
--- env, and serializing those captured envs is exponential in constructor
--- count (the same known issue as record-of-closures `field_access`;
--- see AGENTS.md "Runtime fix (field-access)"). The Rust mirror in
--- `types.rs` remains authoritative until that is fixed. `hnl run` on
--- multi-statement programs containing `data` is also broken upstream
--- (even `data Nat = Zero | Succ(Nat)` fails with "synth_function: node
--- has no children array"), independent of this file.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Pred — symbolic predicates over values (mirror of `types.rs::Pred`)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Semantics (Rust `Pred::eval`, fail-closed: unevaluable ⇒ false):
--   True / False          constants
--   Sorted(list)          the array named `list` is sorted (non-decreasing)
--   LengthEq(a, b)        |a| = |b|        LengthLe(a, b)   |a| <= |b|
--   LengthPlusOne(a, b)   |a| = |b| + 1    LengthSubOne(a, b) |a| = |b| - 1
--   AllSatisfy(list, p)   every element of `list` satisfies predicate `p`
--   Le(a, b)              numeric a <= b
--   HeadOf(elem, list)    `elem` is the first element of `list`
--   IsPerm(a, b)          `a` is a permutation of `b` (same multiset)
--   IsSuccess(v)/IsError(v) `v` is an Ok/Err Result (`__choice__`/ok/err
--                         field convention — see `Pred::eval`)
--   And / Or / Implies    logical combinators (recursive `Pred` payloads)
--   Forall(var, list, p)  `forall var in list, p(var)` — surface syntax
--                         `forall x in list, p(x)`
--   Deterministic(op)     output of `op` is a pure function of its declared
--                         inputs — same inputs ⇒ same output. Added for the
--                         `rand.seeded_*` guarantees (see `rand/rand.hnl`);
--                         not yet present in the Rust mirror.

data Pred :: True|False|Sorted(list: Name)|LengthEq(a: Name, b: Name)|LengthLe(a: Name, b: Name)|AllSatisfy(list: Name, pred: Name)|Le(a: Name, b: Name)|HeadOf(elem: Name, list: Name)|LengthPlusOne(a: Name, b: Name)|LengthSubOne(a: Name, b: Name)|IsPerm(a: Name, b: Name)|IsSuccess(value: Name)|IsError(value: Name)|And(lhs: Pred, rhs: Pred)|Or(lhs: Pred, rhs: Pred)|Implies(lhs: Pred, rhs: Pred)|Forall(var: Name, list: Name, pred: Name)|Deterministic(op: Name)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Laws of the Pred algebra (documentation only — the canonical grammar has
-- `law` but no `axiom`-clause support; stated as comments per the `time.hnl`
-- LAW precedent, and mirrored by `Pred::simplify`/`Pred::eval` in Rust):
--
--   LAW: And(True, p) = p = And(p, True)          (identity)
--   LAW: And(False, _) = False = And(_, False)    (annihilation)
--   LAW: And(p, p) = p                            (idempotence — required
--        for fixpoint convergence of the toy implication checker)
--   LAW: Or(False, p) = p = Or(p, False)
--   LAW: Or(True, _) = True = Or(_, True)
--   LAW: Implies(True, p) = p ; Implies(_, True) = True ; Implies(False, _) = True
--   LAW: Eval semantics — `==>` is material implication: `!p || q`.
--   LAW: Predicates that cannot be evaluated against a value fail closed
--        (evaluate to False) — e.g. `Sorted` on a non-array.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
